

- Monolith Architecture: 
all the modules built into a single codebase and each time one has to build the while code for deployment etc.

- Microservices: 
different modules or services are created and maintained for different purposes so that we achieve "Separation of concerns"/"Single Responsibility Principal". This way we only build the code that is needed and not all the code.
this way diff servervices can maintain their own code and can follow their own CI-CD differently.

- different services are deployed on different ports and from there they can interact with each other by calling different that port/url

e.g.:

UI =>  :/1234 => something.com/
BE =>  :/1000 => something.com/api
SMS => :/2000 => something.com/sms

- useEffect: will be called first after the first render of the component is done 